  "sourceFindings": [
    "Optional layer-aware key is used consistently for MST disjoint-set identity and equal-neighbor skipping. Default bare-XY behavior remains available unchanged. Layer sets are sorted and deduplicated; explicit preconnections remain honored.",
    "Only Pipeline9 true opt-in supplies the key, native-via-landing restoration and same-layer terminal stitching identity. The final stitching adaptation is restricted further to coincident global XY and distinct terminal Z.",
    "Native A03 and B01 two-state same-cell layer transitions carry a single existing planned via; native exporter endpoint substitution loses its two landing coordinates. The exact two-point/single-via/coincident-endpoint/distinct-Z adapter restores those existing landing coordinates before native improvement and stitching, without choosing a new via.",
    "Cold ledger has exactly nine fields. It describes intermediate conceptual MST requirement coverage before preconnection filtering, not final copper continuity or literal preservation of every same-layer alias point identifier."
  ],
